{"name":"Shell Ginger","hex":"#f9e4d6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shell ginger","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An East Asian plant related to ginger, Alpinia zerumbet, grown for its showy flowers, which are shell-pink on the outside and intensely orange and red on the inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell_ginger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpinia zerumbet","blocks":[{"text":"Alpinia zerumbet, commonly known as shell ginger among other names, is a perennial species of ginger native to East Asia. The plants can grow up to 2.5 to 3 meters tall and bear colorful funnel-shaped flowers. They are grown as ornamentals and their leaves are used in cuisine and traditional medicine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/200410_Alpinia_zerumbet_1.JPG/330px-200410_Alpinia_zerumbet_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpinia_zerumbet","wikidata":"Q2703227"},{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Alpinia_zerumbet_pods.jpg/500px-Alpinia_zerumbet_pods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Alpinia_zerumbet_pods.jpg/500px-Alpinia_zerumbet_